# This file has no structure, and it is not meant to acquire one.
#
# Nothing written here is counted, exported, or read by any org-scribe
# command.  The word count walks the manuscript only; compilation reads
# the manuscript only; the entity resolvers work from fixed file names,
# so a character sketched here stays invisible to the linking layer until
# you move it somewhere real.  Sketch someone who may not exist.  Draft a
# scene you will throw away.  Ask the stupid question.  Argue with
# yourself in writing.
#
# Refile what survives with C-c C-w, which offers every heading in every
# file of the project.  Delete the rest without ceremony.
#
# Open this file from anywhere in the project with F8 F8 o.
#
#
# BRANCHING A QUESTION
#
# When a question turns out to have more than one answer, give it a
# heading and tag it :branch:.  Each answer is a child heading carrying a
# state, cycled with C-c C-t:
#
#   OPEN       still live, not yet explored
#   EXPLORING  being written out right now
#   CHOSEN     this is the one
#   REJECTED   ruled out, with the reason kept
#
# Keep rejected branches.  Why-not is worth as much as why, and deleting
# one only means re-deriving it in three months.  REJECTED and CHOSEN are
# done states, so a settled question folds away without losing its
# reasoning.
#
# The outcomes of an answer are that answer's children.  Nest as deep as
# the question actually goes.
#
# These four keywords are deliberately outside the project's TODO
# vocabulary, so an open question never turns up in the TODO search
# (F8 F8 5).  Speculation is not work in progress.
#
# :ABOUT: holds an ID link to whatever the question concerns — a
# character, a thread, a scene — so the question is reachable from that
# side too, and survives a rename.  Leave it empty when the question is
# not yet about anything in particular.
#
# The shape below is an example.  Copy it, or delete it once you have
# your own.

* Loose ideas


* What if <the question>?                                          :branch:
:PROPERTIES:
:ABOUT:
:END:

# What makes this a real question, and what is at stake in the answer.

** OPEN A. <first answer>

*** OPEN <an outcome of A, if it has one>

** OPEN B. <second answer>

** OPEN C. <third answer>
